Please redesign ONLY the existing website Header / Navbar area.

Do NOT change the rest of the page.

Use the existing Header/Navbar component and keep:
- existing logo position
- existing navigation structure
- existing links
- existing spacing/layout logic
- existing responsive/mobile behavior
- all page content below the header

Do not rebuild the header from scratch.

A rock texture image already exists at:

/public/images/rock-texture.jpg

Use this image only as the visual background texture for the Header/Navbar.

VISUAL GOAL

The header should visually match the existing Tibetan rock-art icon system used on the website.

The existing icons have:
- muted warm brown / ochre strokes
- dusty hand-drawn texture
- archaeological / ancient visual language
- soft grain
- low saturation
- weathered rock-art feeling

The header should support these icons instead of competing with them.

Do NOT make the header look photorealistic.

The final surface should feel like:
- dark grey-brown weathered stone
- matte and dusty
- softly blurred
- granular
- slightly uneven
- archaeological
- aged
- natural

Avoid:
- sharp realistic rock photography
- marble
- polished stone
- concrete
- dramatic cave lighting
- fantasy game stone walls
- artificial digital noise
- high contrast cracks
- glossy effects


BACKGROUND IMAGE

Use:

background-image: url('/images/rock-texture.jpg');
background-size: cover;
background-repeat: no-repeat;

Choose a background-position that keeps visually useful stone texture visible.

Do not zoom/crop the image too aggressively.

Because the source image may be too photographic, soften it visually using overlays rather than changing the image itself.


DARK WARM OVERLAY

Add a warm dark overlay above the rock image:

rgba(24, 22, 20, 0.45)

The stone surface should remain visible underneath.

The result should be low contrast and soft.


SOFT WEATHERING / BLUR EFFECT

Add subtle CSS layers to make the rock texture feel less photographic.

Use:
- very subtle blur-like softness through translucent overlays
- low-opacity gradients
- muted contrast
- slightly warm brown tint

Do not blur navigation text or logo.

Only visually soften the background layers.


GRAIN

Add a subtle embedded grain layer using ::before or ::after.

The grain should feel like small particles inside the stone surface.

Use:
- tiny warm light particles
- tiny dark particles
- irregular spacing
- different particle sizes
- very low opacity

Avoid uniform film grain.

It should not look animated.

It should feel like dusty stone particles.


IRREGULAR WEATHERING

Add subtle irregular radial gradients.

For example:
- soft darker patch near one side
- soft warmer patch near another side
- slight unevenness across the header

Keep opacity very low.

The goal is natural weathering, not dramatic lighting.


