NAVIGATION TEXT

Keep existing typography unless changing color is necessary.

Use a warm sandstone/off-white color:

rgba(240, 227, 200, 0.9)

Text should remain highly readable.


NAVIGATION HOVER

Add only a subtle hover effect.

On hover:
- slightly brighten text
- reveal a thin underline
- underline animates left to right

The underline should look understated, like a small carved or painted rock-art line.

Example thickness:
1px

Avoid large modern UI animations.


HEADER DEPTH

Add a subtle inset shadow near the bottom:

box-shadow:
inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.04),
inset 0 -8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);

Do not use strong external drop shadows.


IMPORTANT LAYERING

Structure the Header visually like:

rock image
↓
warm dark overlay
↓
subtle weathering gradients
↓
subtle grain layer
↓
logo + navigation content

Make sure the pseudo-elements stay behind the navigation content.

Use:
position: relative;
isolation: isolate;

and appropriate z-index values.


MOBILE

Preserve the existing mobile navigation behavior.

On smaller screens:
- keep the rock texture visible
- use a less aggressive background crop
- keep text/buttons readable
- do not change the existing menu logic

Consider changing only background-position on mobile if needed.


